Optional voice (voice/ and code that loads it on request):
- voice/en_US-kristin-medium.fp16.onnx is derived from the en_US-kristin-medium Piper voice
  (https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices, MIT), by Bryce Beattie, trained on
  public-domain LibriVox recordings. Its weights are stored as 16-bit floats; the network is unchanged.
- ONNX Runtime Web (MIT) and piper-phonemize / espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) are fetched from public CDNs
  at runtime when the voice is switched on. They are not distributed in this repository.
